Package: normpipe
Type: Package
Title: Population-Referenced Norms with Two Layers of Uncertainty for Any Questionnaire
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes", "Zimmermann", email = "jz@uni-kassel.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Generalization of the norming pipeline of Zimmermann, Kerber,
    Kemper, and Weweck (2026, Getting the Personality Inventory for DSM-5
    ready for clinical practice: Population-representative norms that embrace
    uncertainty). An instrument is described in a configuration file (items
    with their response categories, scales, reference cells, reference sample);
    the pipeline then produces weighted percentile T norms per reporting cell
    with credible bands from a Bayesian bootstrap under a Dirichlet prior over
    the attainable scores (the direct route), continuous-age kernel norms,
    score-conditional and integrated intervals for the individual from
    calibrated graded response models, and the export formats of the scoring
    platform. A transfer module for scales that the reference sample did not
    answer (short-form bridge to full-length scales) is optional. The PID-5
    norms of the original publication are the first use case and are
    reproduced from the configuration in inst/instruments/pid5.
